halo infinite has cheaters progression  woes balancing issues and campaign leaks  let's talk about it  if you didn't know halo infinite's  multiplayer beta is out now and even  though it's being received well by fans  it isn't completely without its issues  players have taken to social media to  report instances of cheating and hacking  in halo infinite and the anti-cheat  police department twitter account found  more than a dozen stores selling cheats  for the game this problem seems to be  more widespread on pc and as a result  players are asking 343 to introduce a  cross-play toggle so that console  players can easily avoid those cheaters  according to the verge halo infinite  uses a quote server-side behavior-based  system to detect cheaters and remove  them from the game as opposed to making  use of a third-party software like easy  anti-cheat or battle eye some amount of  cheating is likely to exist in a  free-to-play multiplayer game like halo  infinite but it remains to be seen what  343 may do to prevent it developers  don't often reveal their anti-cheap  plans because doing so could give the  would-be cheaters hackers a tip-off  and while halo multiplayer is playable  early the campaign is not unless you're  one of these people breaking street date  cutscenes from halo infinite's campaign  have already begun leaking but now with  physical copies of the game beginning to  emerge in the wild it is a good time to  be extra careful when navigating the  internet to avoid spoilers  in other halo infinite news jerry hook  lead designer at 343 industries said on  twitter quote yes i am still playing  halo and feeling everyone's pain on  progression  halo infinite's progression system was  criticized almost immediately after the  game's multiplayer launched on november  15th in short players are upset about  how progression is tied to completing  challenges this system actively  encourages people to play the game to  complete challenges and not necessarily  to help the team or play in a more  natural way which according to players  leads to imbalance luckily 343 has made  changes already like the challenge deck  being updated to better serve players of  all skill levels and more robust updates  are coming later according to hook the  progression issues will be quote at the  top of my list to dig into with the team  when staffers return to the office this  week following a holiday break  another item on 343's list is a reported  balance issue within ranked matches halo  pro lethal took to twitter and said  quote would be nice if infinite ranked  matches were actually meant to match all  players of similar rank with each other  instead of doing dumb team balancing  can't even play with other people  without having people put in the game  who are deaf out of their territory no  fun for them either tbh in other words  please let us play with players of a  similar skill level a bronze ranked  player shouldn't be matched with or  against a gold rank player 343's  community manager replied to the tweet  and said quote we agree and the team is  looking into reports of matchups like  this we'll share more detailed updates  on this when we have them  so hit the comment section and let me  know if you're experiencing some of  these cheaters or weird team balancing  in ranked matches and what you want to  see from future halo infinite updates
 

